    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Yordan Alvarez**, who carries the highest efficiency score at 68.01. Despite facing George Kirby, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start due to his elite 0.464 xwOBA and a +8% efficiency boost from batting in the two-hole. Close behind are **Caleb Durbin** (62.97) and **Junior Caminero** (59.82). **Caleb Durbin** is a priority start today; while he faces Bubba Chandler, his 90% stolen base opportunity profile against a slow-delivery pitcher makes him essential for our scarcity-driven strategy in the SB category. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (58.98) against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, benefiting from a +13% dynamic platoon edge and wind conditions that favor hitters.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Nelson Velazquez**, who fell just short of the lineup with a score of 44.57. While **Nelson Velazquez** showed strong base projections, he was edged out by **Colt Keith** (44.90) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (45.24) due to the team\u2019s current focus on maintaining positional depth for the afternoon games. We are closely monitoring the status of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (58.49); while he benefits from a +10% order boost at leadoff against Matthew Liberatore, he carries a wind-in warning that negatively impacts his output. Furthermore, managers should note that **Gary Sanchez** (47.75) and **Colt Keith** (44.89) face significant headwinds from opposing starters with high-level skill sets\u2014specifically Yamamoto and the L/L matchup respectively\u2014making them marginal starts that require close observation of the final lineup cards.\n\nWith **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** unavailable today due to team off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin, leaving players like **Chase Meidroth** (41.82) on the outside looking in. We are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, so any late-hour changes to batting orders for **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** or **Josh Smith** could fluctuate their scores, particularly for **Josh Smith**, who faces a high-risk assignment against Gerrit Cole. As always, the goal remains aggressive cap management while prioritizing the elite SB potential offered by our secondary options like **Caleb Durbin**.",
